cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, and cite the PLaTypus paper it ports."
title: "platypus-arm64: Restricting Cross-Library Control Flow on AArch64"
abstract: >-
  An AArch64 port of PLaTypus's execution jails: an out-of-tree LLVM 20 pass
  and a per-module start-up routine that clamp indirect-call targets into the
  calling module, relying on Arm BTI, evaluated on an Apple M4 Pro running
  Arm64 Linux.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Patel
    given-names: Aditya
    affiliation: "Indian Institute of Science, Bengaluru"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AdityaPatel2004/platypus-arm64"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-13"
keywords:
  - control-flow integrity
  - AArch64
  - Arm BTI
  - code-reuse attacks
  - LLVM
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "PLaTypus: Restricting Cross-Module Transitions to Mitigate Code-Reuse Attacks"
    authors:
      - family-names: Chatzianagnostou
        given-names: Apostolos
      - family-names: Sanchez Bajo
        given-names: Marcos
      - family-names: Rossow
        given-names: Christian
    conference:
      name: "IEEE Symposium on Security and Privacy (S&P)"
    year: 2026
